 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# JAK2 V617F Molecular Analysis\n","\n","A reproducible educational analysis of the canonical **JAK2 V617F** variant, connecting nucleotide-level representation to protein consequence and molecular diagnostic context.\n","\n","**Variant:** `NM_004972.4:c.1849G>T` → `p.Val617Phe`\n","\n","**dbSNP:** `rs77375493`\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Objectives\n","\n","This notebook will:\n","1. Represent the canonical JAK2 V617F variant using explicit transcript and genome-assembly versions.\n","2. Verify the nucleotide-to-amino-acid consequence.\n","3. Summarize the variant in a machine-readable table.\n","4. Provide a foundation for subsequent database annotation and visualization.\n","\n","> This is a research/educational workflow and not a clinical diagnostic assay.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from dataclasses import dataclass\n","import pandas as pd\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["@dataclass(frozen=True)\n","class VariantRecord:\n","    gene: str\n","    transcript: str\n","    hgvs_c: str\n","    hgvs_p: str\n","    dbsnp: str\n","    assembly: str\n","    genomic_hgvs: str\n","\n","variant = VariantRecord(\n","    gene=\"JAK2\",\n","    transcript=\"NM_004972.4\",\n","    hgvs_c=\"NM_004972.4:c.1849G>T\",\n","    hgvs_p=\"p.Val617Phe\",\n","    dbsnp=\"rs77375493\",\n","    assembly=\"GRCh38\",\n","    genomic_hgvs=\"NC_000009.12:g.5073770G>T\",\n",")\n","variant\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["summary = pd.DataFrame([{\n","    \"Gene\": variant.gene,\n","    \"Transcript\": variant.transcript,\n","    \"HGVS_c\": variant.hgvs_c,\n","    \"HGVS_p\": variant.hgvs_p,\n","    \"dbSNP\": variant.dbsnp,\n","    \"Assembly\": variant.assembly,\n","    \"Genomic_HGVS\": variant.genomic_hgvs,\n","}])\n","summary\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Nucleotide consequence\n","\n","The canonical transcript-level change is **c.1849G>T**. At the protein level this produces **p.Val617Phe (V617F)**.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["reference_nt = \"G\"\n","alternate_nt = \"T\"\n","reference_aa = \"Val\"\n","alternate_aa = \"Phe\"\n","position = 617\n","\n","assert reference_nt != alternate_nt\n","assert position == 617\n","\n","consequence = {\n","    \"reference_nucleotide\": reference_nt,\n","    \"alternate_nucleotide\": alternate_nt,\n","    \"protein_position\": position,\n","    \"reference_amino_acid\": reference_aa,\n","    \"alternate_amino_acid\": alternate_aa,\n","}\n","pd.Series(consequence)\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Diagnostic interpretation framework\n","\n","A molecular result should be integrated with CBC findings, peripheral-blood and bone-marrow morphology, clinical findings, and other molecular markers such as **CALR** and **MPL** when appropriate. A negative JAK2 V617F result does not by itself exclude an MPN.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["driver_genes = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"Gene\": [\"JAK2\", \"CALR\", \"MPL\"],\n","    \"Role\": [\"Major MPN driver; V617F is the focal variant\", \"Alternative canonical MPN driver\", \"Alternative canonical MPN driver\"],\n"})\n","driver_genes\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Reproducibility notes\n","\n","For downstream analyses, retain:\n","- reference genome assembly;\n","- transcript accession/version;\n","- database release/version;\n","- software versions; and\n","- analysis parameters.\n","\n","The next iteration of this notebook will add programmatic retrieval/verification from public resources such as ClinVar, dbSNP, Ensembl and the ClinGen Allele Registry, followed by variant visualization.\n"]}
 ],
